WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
A row of animals watches something happen.

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.840
A shape falls from a tall structure.

3
00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:10.130
Then a small, quick pig skips
up and down in front of them.

4
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.490
He talks, and talks.

5
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.170
By the end, the same animals
believe a different story.

6
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.150
They saw it with their own eyes.

7
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.300
So how are they talked out of it?

8
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:24.850
In this mission, you'll meet Squealer,
the pig who explains Napoleon's decisions

9
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.370
to everyone else.

10
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.310
You'll open his toolkit of
persuasion, one method at a time.

11
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:35.300
And you'll ask whether he works alone,
then test it all on a modern speech outside

12
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:36.610
a library.

13
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.180
Your mission: explain how the animals
are talked out of what they saw.
